594</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Ortuno</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Quesada</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lopez-Claessens</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Castella</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Sanfeliu</surname> <given-names>I</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Anton</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>The role of wild boar (<italic>Sus scrofa</italic>) in the eco-epidemiology of <italic>R. slovaca</italic> in northeastern Spain.</article-title><source>Vector Borne Zoonotic Dis</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>7</volume>:<fpage>59</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>64</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/vbz.2006.0576</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17417958</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Gray</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Stanek</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kundi</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kocianova</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Dimensions of engorging <italic>Ixodes ricinus</italic> as a measure of feeding duration.</article-title><source>Int J Med Microbiol</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>295</volume>:<fpage>567</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>72</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijmm.2005.05.008</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16325552</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Brouqui</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bacellar</surname> <given-names>F</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Baranton</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Birtles</surname> <given-names>RJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bjoersdorff</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Blanco</surname> <given-names>JR</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Guidelines for the diagnosis of tick-borne bacterial diseases in Europe.</article-title><source>Clin Microbiol Infect</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>10</volume>:<fpage>1108</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>32</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1469-0691.2004.01019.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15606643</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>